### C8 — Cooling hardware inside the RPZ, within 2,500 feet of the RWY 19R threshold
**Draft sentence:** "This proposal places the same class of cooling hardware inside the RPZ — within 2,500 feet of the RWY 19R threshold."  
**Basis:** The original argument states the proposal is "within the RWY 19R departure and RWY 1L approach surfaces." The RPZ for a Cat II/III precision instrument runway (visibility minimums below 3/4 mile) extends 2,500 feet from the runway end per AC 150/5300-13B. The claim "within 2,500 feet of the threshold" is therefore an outer-bound inference: if within the RPZ, the facility is necessarily within 2,500 feet (the RPZ outer boundary).  
**Status: Qualified** — "within 2,500 feet" is the maximum possible distance given RPZ membership; the actual measured distance was not documented in a primary source. The claim is accurate as a characterization of RPZ membership and its implication. **Primary source checked: true** (AC 150/5300-13B RPZ dimensions confirmed through regulatory brief).

