## Source-Integrity Problems

**S1 — Quantitative brief / calculations.json conflated two separate cases.** The quantitative-analyst brief and calculations.json attributed the "200-MW, 2.6 miles" specifics to a combined analysis note that mentioned both the Byron Municipal Airport (Mariposa Energy Project) case and the Long Beach Airport (Puente Power Project / CEC 15-AFC-01) case. The strategist merged them into a single sentence, wrongly attributing the Byron-case metrics to the Puente/Long Beach case. Corrected in this pass.

**S2 — Regulatory-political-analyst brief: "10,000-foot" wildlife standard.** The brief cites this as the AC 150/5200-33C zone for stormwater management facilities. Multiple agents reached the same conclusion. However, the primary PDF source was inaccessible during verification and the specific 10,000-foot distance for stormwater facilities (as distinct from landfill units) could not be confirmed. The underlying argument — that an open-water retention basin in an approach corridor violates the AC — is sound, but the specific distance figure was not reproduced in the final draft.

